 "frame": {
  "s1": {
   "locator": "special/Normal.html@sentence:Recall",
   "text": "Recall that in general, if \\(X\\) is a random variable with mean \\(\\mu\\) and standard deviation \\(\\sigma \\gt 0\\), then \\(Z = (X - \\mu) / \\sigma\\) is the standard score of \\(X\\)."
  },
  "s2": {
   "locator": "special/Normal.html@sentence:A corollary",
   "text": "A corollary of the last result is that if \\(X\\) has a normal distribution then the standard score \\(Z\\) has a standard normal distribution."
  },
  "s3": {
   "locator": "special/Normal.html@sentence:Conversely,",
   "text": "Conversely, any normally distributed variable can be constructed from a standard normal variable."
  }
 },
